  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "While EAC can be useful (not by much in a non competitive game like vrchat) you first have to add many fixes and features. Two people I know use being IKTweaks and avatar hider (hides avi’s at certain distances). These two make the experience easier to look at as well as make the game more playable. \n\nNow regarding Anti-Cheat, it is completely useless in this game as malicious modders will always find a way. This may also impact performance so not only will you be removing mods but losing a large proportion of PCVR players, seeing the game almost unplayable then. So tackle possibly putting in your own anti-crash system so players won’t have to mod them in which could help tackle modding crashers. This possibly will not tackle avatar crashers though. \n\nIt is a relaxing social game, not a competitive one so this is completely useless and over board for this game in my complete opinion.\n\nThis is also the one straw that may lead to me leaving VRChat. I left for a fun game but if it shall continue like this I may cancel my plus and spread word of how VRChat is going downhill, please do not make us have to leave the game we all love so much.",
